.TH CHTTPCLI_SET_ENGINE_NUM_REACTOR_THREADS 3 "2026-07-17" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpcli_set_engine_num_reactor_threads \- set the OS thread count for chttpclient's async-engine reactor
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpclient.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpcli_set_engine_num_reactor_threads(size_t num_threads);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Configures how many OS threads the shared Tier 2/3 async-engine
event_loop reactor devotes to its own polling and dispatch, per
event_loop_create_with_mprocs's own num_reactor_threads parameter (see
cthreadcomm.h): 1 means a single thread both polls and dispatches
inline; any larger value means one dedicated polling thread plus
(num_threads - 1) dispatch worker threads.

By default (never having called this function, or having called it
with num_threads == 0), the reactor sizes itself to
sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN), falling back to 1 if that query fails.
Passing a positive num_threads overrides that auto-detection and pins
the reactor to exactly that many threads instead; passing 0 restores
the default auto-detected sizing.  This configures only the shared
reactor's own construction, independent of any individual chttpcli
instance's own settings.

May only be called before the reactor has ever started in this process
(i.e. before the first chttpclient_do_async/_streaming call anywhere),
or after the engine has fully stopped (every chttpcli async user has
released its reference and the automatic teardown has completed).
Unlike chttpsvr_set_engine_num_reactor_threads's typically
process-lifetime reactor, this engine starts and stops on its own as
Tier 2/3 usage comes and goes, so this window recurs naturally rather
than being a one-shot process-startup opportunity.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success on success.
ccol_not_permitted if the engine is currently running; wait for it to
    fully stop first.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpcli_set_engine_mem_mgmt_procs (3),
.BR chttpcli_set_engine_logger (3),
.BR chttpclient_do_async (3),
.BR chttpclient_do_pooled (3),
.BR chttpsvr_set_engine_num_reactor_threads (3)
